From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: 2026-11-06
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: pass the registry root element to VkXML (Python 3.13)

utils_gen.py builds VkXML (an ElementTree Element subclass) from the ElementTree that ET.parse() returns.
Python 3.13 rejects that with "TypeError: expected an Element, not ElementTree"; Python up to 3.12 accepted
it. Hosts whose Python is 3.13 therefore fail to build libplacebo v7.349.0.
Passing the root element works on every Python version.

Upstream-Status: Pending
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Rationale: the generator script has no option to select another input type; the build host's Python is not
  ours to choose (Homebrew and distributions move to 3.13).
---
 src/vulkan/utils_gen.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/utils_gen.py b/src/vulkan/utils_gen.py
index a8652fd..4d55fcd 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/utils_gen.py
+++ b/src/vulkan/utils_gen.py
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@ if __name__ == '__main__':
     if not xmlfile or xmlfile == '':
         xmlfile = find_registry_xml(datadir)
 
-    registry = VkXML(ET.parse(xmlfile))
+    registry = VkXML(ET.parse(xmlfile).getroot())
     with open(outfile, 'w') as f:
         f.write(TEMPLATE.render(
             vkresults = get_vkenum(registry, 'VkResult'),
